Package: riscos-print
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: riscos-support (>= 1.0.0086-1), cups, cups-daemon, cups-client, cups-filters, ghostscript, avahi-daemon, dbus-daemon, ipp-usb
Conflicts: systemd, systemd-sysv, sysvinit-core, udev
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-rolpkg
Description: Printing for RISC OS on Linux, through Linux's CUPS
 RISC OS prints with its own PostScript printer driver to "Linux printer"
 (in !Printers), whose jobs go to Linux's CUPS, which prints them on any
 printer it can use: network printers that need no driver (IPP Everywhere,
 AirPrint: most made since about 2012, found by themselves through avahi)
 and USB printers that speak IPP over USB (ipp-usb). Depends on CUPS,
 cups-filters and Ghostscript (which turn PostScript into what the printer
 takes), avahi and ipp-usb. riscos-support's rol-print starts them (there
 is no systemd here) and hands RISC OS's jobs to CUPS. Configure's "Linux
 printing" plug-in (riscos-harddisc) chooses the printer, adds and removes
 printers and changes their settings. Installing it puts Linux printer in
 !Printers, if !Printers has no printers of its own yet.
